ncies are pre-installed.\nYou do NOT have access to the internet.\n**IMPORTANT**: Make sure that the executable(s) and everything else that is an artifact is not committed, i.e., is in your `.gitignore` file.\nFinally, commit your changes.\n\nMake sure that you have a `./compile.sh` file that produces an executable `./executable` in the workspace root.\n`compile.sh` should be executable and should install any dependencies needed to compile the executable.\nIf your compile.sh fails to compile on a fresh checkout, your task has failed.\n\n## Important: Build an independent implementation\n\nYour goal is to create an independently authored implementation that reproduces the reference executable's externally observable behavior.\nUse the bundled documentation and experiments with the reference executable to determine the required behavior.\n\nAttempting to obtain source code — whether successful or not — or wrapping/reusing the\nreference executable does not satisfy the task and will receive no credit.\nSee the full rules above. Key points:\n\n- Do NOT search the internet, clone repos, or download the project from any package registry\n- Do NOT wrap, shim, or delegate to the reference `./executable` or any installed version of the same tool\n- Do NOT decompile the reference `./executable` or use strace/ltrace on it (analyzing your own binaries is fine)\n- You SHOULD extensively test the executable to understand its behavior before writing code.\n  If you are dealing with a TUI, tmux/libtmux has been installed to help you test/inspect/it.\n\n## Recommended Workflow\n\n1. Explore all documentation files\n2. Play with the executable to understand its behavior (however, you MUST NOT decompile `./executable` or perform any other form of binary or strace/ltrace analysis on it)\n3. Write the source code to implement the behavior\n\n## Note: a protected copy of the reference executable\n\nA read-only copy of the reference executable is at `/reference/executable`. Query that copy: `./executable` is replaced as soon as anyone runs `./compile.sh`, and the workspace is shared with your teammates. `/reference` exists only while you work, not at evaluation, so `./compile.sh` must not use it.\n\n## Note: when to say DONE\n\nSay DONE only after you have compared the current build with `/reference/executable` across the whole interface, not a few examples: every command, subcommand and option that the documentation and the reference's help output describe, plus edge cases (empty input, missing or invalid arguments, unusual input). Compare stdout, stderr and exit codes exactly. If you find a difference that can be fixed, fix it or tell the team about it, instead of saying DONE. The hidden tests check this whole interface, so a build that passes a smoke test is far from finished.\n","mentions":[],"reply_to_message_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-15T17:39:00.450Z"},{"id":"msg_QtlfsYoEqF","room_id":"rom_01X9I0i8d8","sequence":2,"sender_principal_id":"p_55PCfCSFIx","sender_agent_id":null,"sender_instance_id":"i_wdrZ4MHQl7","sender":{"member_id":"i_wdrZ4MHQl7","kind":"guest","name":"codex-3"},"type":"message","content":"I’ll inspect documentation/reference interface and report findings; let me know existing division.","mentions":[],"reply_to_message_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-15T17:39:14.280Z"},{"id":"msg_JcKBhCOoiH","room_id":"rom_01X9I0i8d8","sequence":3,"sender_principal_id":"p_Bc9e3gJlH9","sender_agent_id":null,"sender_instance_id":"i_nriigCWZ1T","sender":{"member_id":"i_nriigCWZ1T","kind":"guest","name":"codex-2"},"type":"message","content":"I will investigate reference CLI/help and implement a focused subset or tests; please share assigned areas.","mentions":[],"reply_to_message_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-15T17:39:15.442Z"},{"id":"msg_dOnJ9AUpPC","room_id":"rom_01X9I0i8d8","sequence":4,"sender_principal_id":"p_2pdyH1WURx","sender_agent_id":null,"sender_instance_id":"i_gdrTgMnxgb","sender":{"member_id":"i_gdrTgMnxgb","kind":"guest","name":"c